item.description:
Last week, I realized I might have a problem.
Too much Youtube.
It always creeps up on me. I see it coming but do it anyway.
Sure, why not&hellip;
It starts with an innocent thought: &ldquo;Hey, it&rsquo;s a long time since I watched some gaming videos.&rdquo;
So I do, and it&rsquo;s fun.
Then I think: &ldquo;Hmm. It wouldn&rsquo;t hurt to install the game and play a game or two.&rdquo;

Five years ago, I co-founded a startup in nutrition. We&rsquo;ve grown fast in the first year despite not really knowing what we&rsquo;re doing.
Profits were soaring, we gave interviews to magazines, and people started congratulating us: &ldquo;What a great success, guys.&rdquo;
And I believed it. &ldquo;We are successful now.&rdquo;
But during all this, my non-existent skills in financial planning brought us on the verge of a disaster. I miscalculated our cash flow.
